  ⚠ KV-05-169: "sprocket-hubspot" es marca registrada de un tercero: uso INTERNO hasta aprobación escrita de HubSpot (formulario con boceto, 7–10 días hábiles). No publicar ni pautar con esta pieza.
IT MUST NOT LOOK AI-GENERATED: a real candid documentary photograph taken by a working photographer on a full-frame mirrorless camera with a real lens. Realism comes from PEOPLE, LIGHT AND MATERIALS, not from dirt: visible skin pores, fine wrinkles, uneven skin tone, stray hairs, natural fabric creases, real paper texture, soft dust visible only in a beam of light, slight motion blur on moving hands, subtle natural lens vignetting, a slightly imperfect un-staged composition. The SPACE is clean, cared-for and organized like a premium creative studio: only one or two lived-in details (a mug, a notebook); NO dirt, NO stains, NO coffee rings, NO loose tape scraps, NO tangled cables, NO mess. No plastic skin, no perfect symmetry, no glossy CGI surfaces, no over-sharpening, no HDR, no beauty retouching, no stock-photo smiles. Natural true-to-life color with no color grading; highlights keep detail, shadows open. Latin American people with real, characterful faces. PRINTED MATTER EXISTS but is never readable: book spines, labels, packaging, papers and screens are present exactly as they would be in any real working room, and they are kept ILLEGIBLE BY PHYSICAL MEANS ONLY — too small, out of focus, cut by the frame edge, at a steep angle, turned away or lost in shadow — NEVER by being blank. NO blank book spines, NO empty labels, NO unmarked packaging, NO featureless screens: a room where nothing at all carries writing reads as fabricated. No logos, no brand marks, no watermarks, and no text sharp enough to actually read.

VISUAL IMPACT (this is an award-level editorial photograph, the kind that stops the scroll): ONE bold visual idea per frame; LIGHT WITH CHARACTER — a hard, directional beam of real sunlight or a single strong source sculpting the subject, with crisp graphic shadows and rich but detailed darks (never flat, never evenly lit); a DECISIVE MOMENT at the peak of the action; a GRAPHIC COMPOSITION with strong geometry, clear figure-ground separation and generous calm negative space; THREE distinct depth planes (blurred foreground, sharp subject, soft background). COLOR: natural true-to-life color, no grading; a restrained palette where bright azure blue (#0375DB) emerges naturally in the spatial composition through scene light, reflections, real materials or the relationship between depth planes, creating graphic rhythm without requiring a separate blue prop; everything else calm and neutral-warm; highlights keep detail; white balance warm-neutral, shadows never blue.

EXTREME CROP — verify it by the cut, not by feeling: the bank of faders runs off the right edge and off the bottom — no console body, no room, no operator is ever visible, only the channel strip itself. The face or object fills the entire frame at this crop: no shoulders, no body, no room around it, at most a sliver of light at one edge. The frame must read as if the photographer was too close for the subject to fit.

HORIZONTAL 16:9 composition. All people and objects stay entirely inside the RIGHT 55% of the frame. TEXT SPACE (planned, essential): the LEFT 42% of the frame is the dark unlit console housing, evenly toned and free of any light, its matte finish visible, a DEEP, warm, evenly toned shadow, deep but ALWAYS keeping visible texture and detail of the material — never a flat pure-black panel, never an evenly filled shape — dark enough for white text, with no objects, windows, light beams or bright spots in it, reserved for a headline; the subject sits in the right half.

IMAGE 1 (object reference): Image 1 is the official 3D sculpture of the HubSpot sprocket symbol. Reproduce EXACTLY this object — same silhouette and same proportions: a ring at the lower right, a short bar going up from it, a long bar at the upper left ending in the larger node, and a short bar at the lower left ending in the smaller node. Solid extrusion of uniform thickness (about a quarter of the ring width), minimal bevel, matte enamel finish in its exact orange with no colour variation. Do NOT add teeth, gears, text or extra parts, do NOT re-proportion it, and do NOT rotate it into an unreadable angle. Ignore its studio background.

SCENE (production suite at night, extreme macro): a long bank of identical channel faders fills the action area of the frame, cropped hard at the right edge. EVERY fader is pulled all the way DOWN to zero — a dead flat line of forty identical caps, their scales unlit. ONE fader, just right of centre, is pushed ALL THE WAY UP: it stands alone above the flat line, its channel strip the only one with a glowing cool blue level showing. The eye lands on that one raised fader first, then reads the dead flat row it is standing in. A hard low raking light from the left skims across the caps and throws a row of sharp parallel shadows; the light dies before it reaches the text area. A small orange sculpture sits at the far right end of the strip, cropped by the edge. 100mm macro lens at f/4, focus on the raised fader. The whole frame is COOL and contemporary: daylight-neutral white balance, blue-leaning shadows, nothing warm, amber, golden or tungsten anywhere, no retro glow — the ONLY warm colour in the entire picture is the small orange sculpture itself. Everything except the sculpture is completely unbranded and no text anywhere is readable: the channel markings are tiny, angled and shallow-focused. CRITICAL FRAMING (horizontal 16:9): the ACTION AREA is the RIGHT 55% of the frame. The LEFT 45% of the frame, top to bottom, is one single dark, evenly toned surface with NOTHING in it: no person, no object, no screen, no lamp, no window, no light beam, no bright spot, no shadow edge. Every person, every object, all the action, all the light and every bright patch stay inside the right 55%.

FOREGROUND (planned): the out-of-focus near edge of the console apron running along the very bottom against the lens, so close to the lens that it dissolves into a soft abstract blur with no visible edges or details, spanning the ENTIRE width of the bottom 16% of the frame (never a hard band), DARK near black, matte; its center calm and even.

